# Kanso web (Vercel) configuration.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. Every variable here is NEXT_PUBLIC_ and
# is therefore compiled into the browser bundle — never put a secret in this
# file. The Supabase service-role key belongs in apps/api only.

# --- Supabase ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API. Both values are browser-safe.
# Leave blank locally: the app boots without them and says so plainly, and the
# /pro/* routes fall back to the development preview.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Backend -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Origin of the FastAPI service on Render, with no trailing slash. next.config.ts
# rewrites /api/* here, so the browser makes a same-origin request and no CORS
# preflight is involved.
#
# Set this locally too — the mechanism is the same in every environment, so no
# host is ever hardcoded in the app. For a local backend started with
# `uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000`, use:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
#
# Left blank, /api/* is not rewritten and API calls will 404 — which is the
# correct signal that the backend is not wired up yet.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# --- Site ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production origin, no trailing slash. Used for absolute URLs in metadata.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
